UID:5726ec1ff7f83a78ad0dfe6b9c96de926e09dfc75ba72cd77c5c38278fcfa7ca@pruts-
 agenda.local
DTSTAMP:20260829T131156Z
SUMMARY:Echoes from Afar: Build your own archive
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
DTSTART:20260912T120000Z
DTEND:20260912T140000Z
DESCRIPTION:We invite you to the hybrid workshop led by Kexin Hong and Yiya
 o Wei\, from Echoes from Afar\, an open-source\, living\, online archive t
 hat explores how digital infrastructures can challenge conventional forms 
 of representation. Their project not only opens space for Asian diasporic 
 communities\, but it also lays the groundwork for a living archive\, allow
 ing richer\, more textured forms of visibility for any project. \nOver the
  past years we’ve seen an increase in censorship\, shadow-banning\, and 
 blocking of accounts across large social media platforms like Instagram. M
 any artists\, designers\, and cultural and social organisations rely on th
 ese platforms to connect with their communities and share their stories an
 d their work. What if we could build our own archives\, websites and netwo
 rks without giving our autonomy away to Big Tech? \n\n\nIn the first part 
 of the workshop\, participants will learn about Echoes from Afar and the b
 asics of self-uploading and managing artworks on the platform\, so that pa
 rticipants can begin contributing their own work if they would like to. \n
 In the second part of the workshop\, we will learn about the open-source w
 orkflow behind the archive\, showing how participants can build their own 
 websites or archives using free and accessible tools that require no prior
  coding experience. Throughout this hands-on process\, the workshop will d
 raw on AI technologies\, such as Claude\, as one of the working tools that
  can assist website building\, while still remaining grounded in a practic
 e of ethical care. \nIn its approach to storytelling\, the project seeks t
 o safeguard the integrity of personal narratives\, to cultivate plurality 
 and openness in how stories surface and circulate. \nThis workshop is hybr
 id\, so you can choose to join onsite in Amsterdam at The Hmm studio or on
 line. \n\n\nRequirements and Prep\nNo prior coding experience is necessary
  and you do not need to be of Asian heritage to join. Please bring your la
 ptop for the workshop. It’s also good to think ahead of time about what 
 kind of archive and website you want to create and collect some texts and 
 images or videos you want to embed in it. \n\n\nThe Hmm experiments…\n\n
 \nThis event is part of a series of programs that we are developing with T
 he Hmm\, where we give space in our studio for our community to explore ne
 w ideas and experiment with workshops as part of our public program. \n\n\
 nWhat you need to know\n\n📅 Date: Saturday 12 September 2026\n🕗 Time
 s: 14.00 – 16.00 CEST\n📍 Location: The Hmm’s studio\, NDSM-plein 12
 5\, 1033 WC Amsterdam\, and online\n🎟 Tickets: €12\,50 regular\, €9
 \,50 students (onsite or online)\n\nAs these workshops are more intimate s
 essions\, there is a limited supply of tickets available. You can find inf
 ormation about physical accessibility at The Hmm’s studio here. \n\n💚
  This programme is kindly supported by the Creative Industries Fund NL
URL:https://thehmm.nl/event/echoes-from-afar-build-your-own-archive/
CATEGORIES:The Hmm
END:VEVENT
