SUMMARY:SOLD OUT! Cyberdeck workshop: build your own 'mesh-berry' 🫐
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
DTSTART:20260926T110000Z
DTEND:20260926T150000Z
DESCRIPTION:Hand-soldered cyberdecks are all over the internet. The cyberde
 cks we know from cyberpunk fiction and hacker culture were improvised mach
 ines—originally appearing in William Gibson’s 1984 novel Neuromancer
 —often built within a narrow and masculine idea of who gets to tinker\, 
 hack\, and build. The cyberdecks filling our feeds today look different. T
 hey’re cute. \nFrom mermaid-shell Raspberry Pis to Hello Kitty makeup ca
 ses\, these devices have exploded in popularity over the past year\, thank
 s to women teaching each other to build artistic\, hyper-feminine computer
 s online. \nCyberdecks push back against the sleek\, sealed\, and extracti
 ve technologies we rely on every day. While most consumer computers lock u
 s into systems that are becoming increasingly unethical\, from non-consens
 ual surveillance to automatic AI integration no one asked for\, cyberdecks
  are hacked together. Often built with femininity and sustainability in mi
 nd\, they’re personalised with cute and colourful items that would other
 wise be thrown away. In an age of mass-produced devices\, cyberdecks turn 
 technology into a form of self-expression. \nMake your personalised ‘mes
 h-berry’! 🫐\nIn this workshop\, you’ll build your very own\, person
 alised ‘mesh-berry’ 🫐 device: a local chat tool that runs on a mesh
  network. You don’t need WiFi\, internet\, or anything Big Tech related.
  To keep things accessible\, we won’t build a full computer\, but focus 
 on a working chat tool you can actually take home and use\, change\, or bu
 ild upon. \nGuided by web developer and artist Heerko van der Kooij\, you
 ’ll learn how to hand-solder your own motherboard and how to style your 
 chat program. Lilian Stolk from The Hmm will go a bit deeper into the aest
 hetic side of things\, looking at how (and why) to design a personal case 
 for your device \nAfter the workshop\, you’ll walk away with a working m
 esh-berry that you can use to chat with other mesh-berry owners nearby. If
  your friends couldn’t make it to this workshop\, you’ll have picked u
 p the skills to build one for them yourself. \nRequirements and Prep\n\nYo
 u don’t need to have any experience with coding to join this workshop. T
 he ticket price includes all the hardware you’ll need: a screen\, keyboa
 rd\, battery\, and speaker. We’ll provide some basic crafting materials\
 , but we ask you to bring your own case that is at least 5x7cm (a bag\, b
 ox\, tin\, or anything else you’d like to turn into your device’s shel
 l) and extra bits and pieces to personalise it further. Think of stickers\
 , fabric\, beads\, paint\, or anything else that makes it yours. The works
 hop will be conducted in English.   \nThe Hmm experiments…\nThis event 
 is part of a series of programs that we are developing with The Hmm\, wher
 e we give space in our studio for our community to explore new ideas and e
 xperiment with workshops as part of our public program. \n\nWhat you need 
 to know\n\n📅 Date: Saturday 26 September 2026\n🕗 Times: 13.00 – 17
 .00 CEST\n📍 Location: The Hmm’s studio\, NDSM-plein 125\, 1033 WC Ams
 terdam\n🎟 Tickets: €45 regular\, €41\,50 students (this is includin
 g €37\,50 for hardware material)\n\nAs these workshops are more intimate
  sessions\, there is a limited supply of tickets available. You can find i
 nformation about physical accessibility at The Hmm’s studio here. \n\n
 💚 This programme is kindly supported by the Creative Industries Fund N
 L
URL:https://thehmm.nl/event/cyberdeck-workshop-build-your-own-mesh-berry-%f
 0%9f%ab%90/
CATEGORIES:The Hmm
END:VEVENT
