SUMMARY:The nature of our monetary system
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
DTSTART:20261025T113000Z
DTEND:20261025T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:In this edition of Good Money\, we return to what money should 
 be at its core: the public technology for organising labour and production
 . How can we create a better world\, in which money does not first have to
  be ‘made’ through polluting and extractive activities?
LOCATION:Waag Futurelab\, Nieuwmarkt 4\, 1012CR Amsterdam
URL:https://waag.org/en/event/nature-our-monetary-system
CATEGORIES:Waag
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7fa32419d9094e8eda459f241a4df7383b08178f5a539ff8d45863d744b2f764@pruts-
 agenda.local
DTSTAMP:20260829T131156Z
SUMMARY:The Hmm @ Brainwash Festival
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
DTSTART:20261031T180000Z
DTEND:20261031T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Townhall: From doom scroll to hope core \nWe’ve all heard the
  diagnosis. Algorithms are rotting our brains\, shortening our attention s
 pans\, and turning us into passive consumers of an endless feed. But what 
 does the evidence actually say? And more importantly: what do we want to d
 o about it? \nIn the last ten years\, the chronological timeline gave way 
 to the algorithmic feed\, and with it\, the way we think\, communicate\, a
 nd tell stories shifted with it. We consume more content than ever\, but d
 o we recognise what’s authentic anymore? And is there anything worth sav
 ing in a life mediated by social media\, ChatGPT\, and an app for everythi
 ng? \nThese are the questions we’re bringing to Brainwash Festival. As p
 art of the “technology = god” programme strand\, we’re hosting a Tow
 nhall that asks: when does convenience become obedience\, and who’s actu
 ally in control? \nAbout Brainwash Festival\nBrainwash Festival is the pla
 ce to be for thought-provoking ideas and visions of the future. At Brainwa
 sh Festival\, philosophers\, scientists\, artists and writers come togethe
 r to explore the big questions of our time and challenge the status quo. W
 e bring together established figures and new voices. We celebrate thinking
 \, doubt and your curiosity. \nBrainwash Festival 2026 takes up the theme 
 ‘the shape of us’\, through which it explores\, from different perspec
 tives\, what it means to live together. \nMore information about the progr
 amme TBA. \n📅 Date: 31 October\n📍 Tolhuistuin\n🎟️ Tickets: via 
 Brainwash \n♿ Accessibility notes\nFind more info on the Tolhuistuin web
 site.
URL:https://thehmm.nl/event/the-hmm-brainwash-festival/
CATEGORIES:The Hmm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6b5b0e0ebc710ab42e4e9025d504e4db242ae31a3570e50140c9790dc661a331@pruts-
 agenda.local
DTSTAMP:20260829T131156Z
SUMMARY:Cyberdeck workshop: build your own 'mesh-berry' #2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
DTSTART:20261107T120000Z
DTEND:20261107T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Hand-soldered cyberdecks are all over the internet. The cyberde
 cks we know from cyberpunk fiction and hacker culture were improvised mach
 ines—originally appearing in William Gibson’s 1984 novel Neuromancer
 —often built within a narrow and masculine idea of who gets to tinker\, 
 hack\, and build. The cyberdecks filling our feeds today look different. T
 hey’re cute. \nFrom mermaid-shell Raspberry Pis to Hello Kitty makeup ca
 ses\, these devices have exploded in popularity over the past year\, thank
 s to women teaching each other to build artistic\, hyper-feminine computer
 s online. \nCyberdecks push back against the sleek\, sealed\, and extracti
 ve technologies we rely on every day. While most consumer computers lock u
 s into systems that are becoming increasingly unethical\, from non-consens
 ual surveillance to automatic AI integration no one asked for\, cyberdecks
  are hacked together. Often built with femininity and sustainability in mi
 nd\, they’re personalised with cute and colourful items that would other
 wise be thrown away. In an age of mass-produced devices\, cyberdecks turn 
 technology into a form of self-expression. \nMake your personalised ‘mes
 h-berry’! 🫐\nIn this workshop\, you’ll build your very own\, person
 alised ‘mesh-berry’ 🫐 device: a local chat tool that runs on a mesh
  network. You don’t need WiFi\, internet\, or anything Big Tech related.
  To keep things accessible\, we won’t build a full computer\, but focus 
 on a working chat tool you can actually take home and use\, change\, or bu
 ild upon. \nGuided by web developer and artist Heerko van der Kooij\, you
 ’ll learn how to hand-solder your own motherboard and how to style your 
 chat program. Lilian Stolk from The Hmm will go a bit deeper into the aest
 hetic side of things\, looking at how (and why) to design a personal case 
 for your device \nAfter the workshop\, you’ll walk away with a working m
 esh-berry that you can use to chat with other mesh-berry owners nearby. If
  your friends couldn’t make it to this workshop\, you’ll have picked u
 p the skills to build one for them yourself. \nRequirements and Prep\n\nYo
 u don’t need to have any experience with coding to join this workshop. T
 he ticket price includes all the hardware you’ll need: a screen\, keyboa
 rd\, battery\, and speaker. We’ll provide some basic crafting materials\
 , but we ask you to bring your own case that is at least 5x7cm (a bag\, b
 ox\, tin\, or anything else you’d like to turn into your device’s shel
 l) and extra bits and pieces to personalise it further. Think of stickers\
 , fabric\, beads\, paint\, or anything else that makes it yours. The works
 hop will be conducted in English. Please feel free to join us\, but don’
 t wait to long. Our first workshop sold out fast. \nThe Hmm experiments…
 \nThis event is part of a series of programs that we are developing with T
 he Hmm\, where we give space in our studio for our community to explore ne
 w ideas and experiment with workshops as part of our public program. \n\nW
 hat you need to know\n\n📅 Date: Saturday 26 September 2026\n🕗 Times:
  13.00 – 17.00 CEST\n📍 Location: The Hmm’s studio\, NDSM-plein 125\
 , 1033 WC Amsterdam\n🎟 Tickets: €55 regular\, €51\,50 students (thi
 s is including €47\,50 for hardware material)\n\nAs these workshops are 
 more intimate sessions\, there is a limited supply of tickets available. Y
 ou can find information about physical accessibility at The Hmm’s studio
  here. \n\n💚 This programme is kindly supported by the Creative Indust
 ries Fund NL
URL:https://thehmm.nl/event/cyberdeck-workshop-build-your-own-mesh-berry-2/
CATEGORIES:The Hmm
END:VEVENT
